      trivia: "【From Refugee to Maestro】Rafael Nodal is a Cuban refugee who crossed to the United States after four days adrift in the 1980 Mariel boatlift, and was originally a classically trained violinist. That musical sensibility is engraved on his brands in vitola names drawn from the language of music — Concerto, Vibrato, Maestro. 【The Crowning Cigar】In 2019 the Maestro of the Quattro Nicaragua was crowned Cigar Aficionado's No. 1 cigar of the year (96 points) — a Nicaraguan puro made by AJ Fernandez of Estelí."
